## 6. Tenancy runtime (backend)

### 6.1 New module layout

```
apps/backend/src/tenancy/
  tenancy.module.ts
  tenant-context.ts           // ALS, requireTenant(), runWithTenant()
  tenant.middleware.ts        // host → tenant, status check, base-domain aliases
  tenant.guard.ts             // @SkipTenant support
  tenant-registry.service.ts  // in-memory host map + platform sync + pub/sub
  tenant-prisma.manager.ts    // LRU PrismaClient per tenant
  tenant-prisma.proxy.ts      // PrismaService/baPrisma forwarding
  tenant-cors.service.ts      // origin allowlist per tenant + base domains
  tenant-bootstrap.service.ts // seed a new tenant
  rls-coverage.service.ts     // fail-fast verification
  tenant-usage.service.ts     // counters + platform sync
  domain-config.service.ts    // primary/base/fallback domains, canonical + alias logic
```

Future (with central commerce): `external-store.resolver.ts`, `tenant-store-job.runner.ts`.

### 6.2 PrismaService refactor

Current: `apps/backend/src/prisma/prisma.service.ts` extends `PrismaClient`, reads `DATABASE_URL`, heals schema, seeds.

Target:
- `PrismaService` becomes a facade/proxy:
  ```ts
  @Injectable()
  export class PrismaService {
    constructor(private manager: TenantPrismaManager) {
      return new Proxy(this, {
        get: (target, prop, receiver) => {
          if (prop in target) return Reflect.get(target, prop, receiver);
          const client = this.manager.getClient(requireTenant().tenantId);
          const value = (client as any)[prop];
          return typeof value === 'function' ? value.bind(client) : value;
        },
      });
    }
  }
  export interface PrismaService extends PrismaClient {}
  ```
- Keep `isRestoreWriteBlocked` semantics? Restore is platform-level; tenant runtime should not expose restore controls.
- Prototype the proxy typing/runtime in Phase 2 before mass codemods. Fallback if the proxy is unstable: expose `get client()` and codemod `this.prisma.` → `this.prisma.client.` with ts-morph.

### 6.3 Better Auth

Current singleton `auth` + global `baPrisma` cannot work with shared multi-tenancy.

Target:
- `createAuthForTenant(tenantId, prisma, host)` factory; cache per `(tenantId, host)`.
- `baPrisma` becomes a proxy to the current tenant client.
- `main.ts` Better Auth handler resolves tenant from Host and calls `getAuthForTenant(...).handler(req)`.
- `DualModeAuthGuard` uses `getAuthForTenant(...).api.getSession`.
- `customSession` queries use the passed tenant client, not global.
- `baseURL`/`trustedOrigins` per tenant domain, including all base domains and verified custom domains; cookies host-scoped (never a wildcard domain).
- Same email can exist in two tenants — validate with a two-tenant auth test.
- `auth.service.ts`, `users.service.ts`, `employees.service.ts`, `customer-linking.service.ts` continue to use `baPrisma` proxy.

### 6.4 Background jobs and intervals

Every queue/interval must run with a tenant context.

**Existing 8 queues:** `email`, `media`, `import`, `tracking`, `marketing`, `backup`, `security-dashboard`, `courier-settlement-import` — every job payload gets `tenantId`; processor wraps handler in `runWithTenant(tenantId, ...)`.

| Area | Files / change |
|---|---|
| Intervals | auth cleanup, blocked-entries expiry, security cleanup, cache cleanup, rate-limit cleanup, page-view buffer, outbox relay, reconciler, retention cleanup, courier webhook cleanup, backup timer, security-dashboard retention — convert to tenant fan-out or platform-only |
| Raw SQL aggregates | `security-dashboard/services/event-aggregator.service.ts`, `dashboard-query.service.ts`, `analytics` — add tenant predicates / iterate tenants |
| Tracking | `page-view-buffer`, `outbox-relay`, `reconciler`, `retention-cleanup` — per-tenant |
| Cache/rate limit | Prefix all Redis keys with `t:<tenantId>:`; cache purge scoped to current tenant (platform admin can purge all) |
| IP block | Move `IpBlockMiddleware` after `TenantMiddleware`; blocks are tenant-scoped |
| Media | Storage paths `uploads/<tenantId>/...`; media queue payload tenantId |

Future central commerce adds 6 store queues; see §3.12.6.

Add a `TenantJobRunner` helper:
```ts
await tenantJobRunner.forEachActiveTenant(async (tenantId) => {
  await runWithTenant({ tenantId }, () => service.run());
});
```
Paginate tenants; never load all at once.

### 6.5 Backups / export

- Remove tenant-facing `pg_dump`/restore. A tenant admin must never trigger a full-DB dump.
- `BackupService` becomes platform-only or is removed from the tenant app.
- New `TenantExportService` / `scripts/saas/export-tenant.ts`:
  - sets `app.tenant_id`, iterates all tenant tables in dependency order, writes JSON/CSV + media zip.
  - used by platform admin for support/offboarding.
- Tenant-facing `db_backup` feature becomes "Data export" (bounded, async, emailed link).
- Platform full backup + PITR covers disaster recovery.

### 6.6 Media, storage, mobile

- Local volume and R2 both use `tenantId/` prefix.
- URLs: `/uploads/<tenantId>/<uuid>.<ext>`; public product media remains public, private files require authenticated tenant access.
- Media derivative queue jobs carry tenantId.
- Mobile builder jobs carry tenant host/config and store artifacts under `tenantId/`; feature-gated (`mobile_distribution*`).
- POS PWA is served per origin (`/pos/`), so service-worker scope is naturally tenant-specific.

