## 9. Testing and verification

### 9.1 Tenant isolation (must be automated, CI-blocking)

- Tenant A reads/writes/deletes Tenant B rows through Prisma → zero/404.
- Raw SQL `SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE` without/with wrong tenant → zero rows.
- Insert without tenant context → exception.
- Attempt to change `tenant_id` → trigger restores/rejects.
- Same slug/email/code/idempotencyKey in two tenants → both valid; lookups resolve per tenant.
- Login on wrong tenant host → 401.
- Storefront host A never serves host B config/product/cache.
- Background job for tenant A never touches tenant B.
- Alias base domain A resolves tenant A; a different tenant cannot claim the same slug on another base.
- Fallback domain never routes an unknown host to a tenant.

### 9.2 Functional

- Platform: dynamic plan CRUD/versioning, public pricing, tenant lifecycle, impersonation/audit, domain config.
- Entitlements: feature on/off, plan change invalidation, fallback snapshot, read-only/suspended states.
- Billing: invoice, proof, approve/reject, partial/overpayment, renewal/grace/suspend.
- Custom domain: add/verify/TLS/route/remove; CNAME target configurable.
- Domains: primary, multiple base domains, fallback, canonical/alias redirects, reserved slugs.
- Limits: products/users/orders/warehouses/storage, warning/block/override.
- Storefront/admin/POS parity on two tenants.
- Existing test suites remain green (backend/admin/storefront/POS) with the tenant test harness.

### 9.3 Non-functional

- Load: 50–200 simulated tenants, mixed read/write, pool saturation, slow tenant isolation, alias/fallback routing.
- Backup/restore: full platform+tenant DB, per-tenant export, purge.
- Security: dependency scan, secret scan, OWASP, RLS penetration test, cookie/CORS checks, domain/TLS validation.
- Observability: every log line has tenantId; dashboards show per-tenant error/latency; domain/TLS health.

