## 11. Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Cross-tenant leak via missed query/raw SQL | RLS as hard boundary + non-owner app role + two-tenant isolation suite + no BYPASSRLS in runtime |
| RLS + pooling misconfiguration | Per-tenant pools with startup GUC; session-mode PgBouncer only; assert tenant setting on connect; load test |
| Better Auth per-tenant email uniqueness | Prototype early; delegate proxy/`findFirst` shim; two-tenant auth test |
| Prisma proxy typing/runtime | Spike before codemods; fallback `prisma.client` codemod |
| Storefront cache leakage | Dynamic rendering + host-aware tenant tags + two-host E2E; no shared full-route cache |
| Background job misses tenant | Job payload contract + queue audit + processor wrapper + per-tenant tests |
| ~201-model schema edit errors | Scripted edits + review checkpoints + baseline fresh DB + `prisma validate` + snapshot diff |
| Existing test suite breakage | Global tenant test harness; run suite after each sub-phase; fix TypeScript-guided |
| Noisy neighbor | Per-tenant rate limits, query timeouts, limits, pool caps, load test |
| Shared-DB backup/offboarding | Platform PITR + per-tenant export/purge; never expose `pg_dump` to tenants |
| Manual billing fraud/abuse | Proof review, duplicate transaction ID, audit, amount cross-check, credits |
| SaaS admin compromise | Separate domain/auth, MFA, roles, IP allowlist optional, audit, no direct tenant DB access |
| Plan edits changing existing customers | Immutable `PlanVersion` + explicit "apply to existing" action |
| Custom domain TLS failure | DNS polling, status UI, retries, Caddy ask endpoint, manual override in SaaS admin |
| Domain/alias confusion | Primary/base/fallback validation; canonical redirects; 404 for unknown hosts; reserved slugs across all bases |
| Fallback domain outage | Health checks, monitoring, fallback used only for absolute URLs, never as a tenant guess |
| Central-commerce port divergence | Deferred until upstream is final; additive migrations with tenantId/RLS from day one; §3.12.7 checklist |
| Two-product divergence (old repo) | Decide archive/LTS; no dual maintenance by default; central-commerce port commit + checklist |

